// The revive example of mandocs/drafts/reactive-script-semantics.md, as the
// session its replay plays. reactive/revive.world goes further.
----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let b_moved = b

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

set b = 500

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let c = b + 1

----------
expect all four units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 500 |
| 2 | takes `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `b_moved` = 125 |
| 3 | revives `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 501 |

----------
repl-command
----------

/edit 3 set b = 500
let x = y

----------
expect unit 3 is broken
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 revived `b` when it last ran, and is retracted | `b` taken |
| 2 | takes `b` (1) | reruns | rerun: takes `b`, which unit 1 rebuilt | `b_moved` = 125 |
| 3 | revives `b` (1) | recompile fails | edited | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | recompile fails | `b` was given away by unit 2 | - |

----------
repl-command
----------

/edit 3 set b = 500

----------
expect unit 3 is fixed
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | unit 3 overwrites `b` without reading it | `b` = 500 |
| 2 | takes `b` (1) | untouched | nothing it uses changed | `b_moved` = 125 |
| 3 | revives `b` (1) | recompiles, runs | edited | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | `b` can be named again, as it could in step 1, whose compile is still memoized | `c` = 501 |
